e":"7300","slot":{"zh":"护甲","en":"Armor"}},{"id":"WP1012202","name":{"zh":"发簪","en":"Hairpin"},"level":"1","description":{"zh":"固定头发的工具，既美观也实用，随处可见。","en":"A tool for securing hair, both decorative and practical, seen everywhere."},"evade":"3","price":"2000","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{"father":{"label":{"zh":"父亲","en":"Father"},"people":[{"id":"WJ10631","code":"0"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI102915","name":{"zh":"吴郡陆氏","en":"The Lu clan of Wu Commandery"},"years":["180","999"],"desc":{"zh":"出自妫姓，齐宣王少子通封于平原陆乡，后裔以乡为氏，吴郡顶级望族。江东首望，和顾、朱、张一起被称为“吴中四姓”。陆逊为东吴丞相、大都督，夷陵之战大破刘备；陆抗、陆机、陆云皆一时人杰。白马之祸后家族受挫，唐亡后逐渐迁徙分化。","en":"Descended from the Gui surname, when King Xuan of Qi's youngest son Tong was enfeoffed at Lu Township in Pingyuan, his descendants adopted the township as their surname, becoming a premier aristocratic clan of Wu Commandery. Renowned as the foremost clan of Jiangdong, they were hailed alongside the Gu, Zhu, and Zhang as the 'Four Great Clans of Wu'. Lu Xun served Eastern Wu as Chancellor and Grand Viceroy, decisively defeating Liu Bei at the Battle of Yiling, Lu Kang, Lu Ji, and Lu Yun were all outstanding figures of their eras. Following the Baima Station Massacre, the Family suffered setbacks, gradually migrating and branching off after the fall of the Tang dynasty."},"talent":{"military":"9","commerce":"7","politics":"8"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":null,"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[[["WJ10514","小女子"],["WJ10514","小女子"],["WJ10514","This humble maiden"],["WJ10514","私め"],["WJ10514","소녀"]]],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"33","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1053","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"0","role":0,"stats":[22,33,71,70,82,75],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"0","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1007102","armor":"WP1014802","helmet":"WP1012202"},"